EMBERIZA
A browser interface for bacpipe.

This product includes software developed by the bacpipe authors
(https://github.com/bioacoustic-ai/bacpipe), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

  bacpipe: A Python package to make bioacoustic deep learning models accessible.
  Vincent S. Kather, Sylvain Haupert, Burooj Ghani and Dan Stowell (2026).
  Methods in Ecology and Evolution. doi:10.1111/2041-210X.70406

The folder app/py/bacpipe/ holds files of bacpipe 1.3.5, copied unchanged from commit
d7aa3a2971ae4287c9f4a10acde324519776296a. app/py/bacpipe/VENDORED.json lists each file with its SHA-256.
The copy is a subset: the 25 other models, the tests, the example notebooks, the type stubs and the logo
images are left out. No file in that folder is modified. bacpipe's own licence is app/py/bacpipe/LICENSE.

Changes made by EMBERIZA, all outside that folder:
  - bacpipe's pipeline is driven step by step (app/py/emberiza/engine.py) so that the neural networks can run in
    ONNX Runtime Web. The calls, their order and their arguments are those of bacpipe.play().
  - Libraries that cannot be installed in a browser are replaced by stand-ins that do what bacpipe needs from
    them (app/py/shims/, app/py/emberiza/replay.py).
  - Six bacpipe functions that only draw picture files are replaced by functions that do nothing
    (the list DRAWING_ONLY in app/py/emberiza/engine.py).

app/py/emberiza/umap_port.py is a port of parts of umap-learn 0.5.12
(https://github.com/lmcinnes/umap), Copyright (c) 2017, Leland McInnes, BSD 3-Clause License.
The licence text is in LICENSES.md.

